// THE PLANS THAT SURVIVED THE 2026-11-08 RESET (gunbc.design_ruling::plans_reset_and_audit_recommendations_2026_11_08):
// only plans a live consumer reads. Every other gunbc.plans carrier was deleted; git history keeps them.
// Four more are retained because a structured reference still binds them (review of gunbc#16107):
// input_envelope_roadmap (gunbc.ci.ci_input_envelope scaffold bind), fabric_serving_router (a recurring
// failure mode's evidence), fleet_subsumption_manual_gaps (gunbc.retained_shell_script dissolves_to) and
// interpreter_kernel_d (v2.compiler.self_host.seed_retention_frontier). fleet_hardware_fact_consumption is an
// active program carrier (three landings on 2026-11-08) and names host_thermal_operating_point as an owning
// program; v2_complexity_capability_parity is a live roadmap carrier (pointer_resolves); read_set_convergence is the
// active T11 / affected-set consolidation program (2026-11-09); fleet_machine_authority is the machine-registry and host-name de-fork program
// (2026-11-10; D1-D13 answered); closure_consolidation is the ci_spec dissolution and selective-generation program
// (2026-11-10); planning_consolidation is the plans-and-roadmap decomposition (D1 to D3 ruled 2026-11-10, D4 to D6 open).
// Each deletes with its last consumer.
data all_plans: List<Plan> = [
  cli_run_hollowing_plan, extdeps_modeling_preflight_plan, demand_engine_program_plan,
  input_envelope_roadmap_plan, fabric_serving_router_plan, fleet_subsumption_manual_gaps_plan, interpreter_kernel_d_plan,
  fleet_hardware_fact_consumption_plan, host_thermal_operating_point_plan, v2_complexity_capability_parity_plan,
  read_set_convergence_plan, fleet_machine_authority_plan, closure_consolidation_plan,
  planning_consolidation_plan,
]
